  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5206b7d8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2 Data Cleaning\n",
    "\n",
    "We further reduce the dataset to include only individuals between the ages of 18 and 65, as this is the relevant population for our analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 69,
   "id": "22eab692",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Filtering Age (18-65)...\n",
      "Removed 63362 rows outside age range.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df_2_2 = df_2_1.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "if 'AGEP' in df_2_2.columns:\n",
    "    print(\"Filtering Age (18-65)...\")\n",
    "    initial_count = len(df_2_2)\n",
    "    df_2_2 = df_2_2[(df_2_2['AGEP'] >= 18) & (df_2_2['AGEP'] <= 65)]\n",
    "    print(f\"Removed {initial_count - len(df_2_2)} rows outside age range.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "65b13e76",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We then apply imputations for the features `OCCP` (Occupation Code), `INDP` (Industry Code), and `COW` (Class of Worker). If any of these values are missing, we impute them with the corresponding code for \"unemployed.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 70,
   "id": "8b1b6cd8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Imputed OCCP with 9920\n",
      "Imputed INDP with 9920\n",
      "Imputed COW with 9\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Imputations for OCCP and INDP\n",
    "for col in ['OCCP', 'INDP']:\n",
    "    if col in df_2_1.columns:\n",
    "            df_2_2[col] = df_2_2[col].fillna(9920)\n",
    "            print(f\"Imputed {col} with 9920\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Imputations for COW\n",
    "if 'COW' in df_2_2.columns:\n",
    "    df_2_2['COW'] = df_2_2['COW'].fillna(9)\n",
    "    print(\"Imputed COW with 9\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "620b2920",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Lastly, we perform a final check for remaining missing values to ensure data consistency before moving on to feature engineering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 71,
   "id": "57869689",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "No missing values found.\n",
      "Data Cleaning Completed.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "missing = df_2_2.isnull().sum()\n",
    "missing = missing[missing > 0]\n",
    "\n",
    "if not missing.empty:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nFound {len(missing)} columns with missing values.\")\n",
    "    missing_pct = (missing / len(df_2_2)) * 100\n",
    "    missing_report = pd.DataFrame({'Missing Count': missing, 'Percentage': missing_pct})\n",
    "    print(missing_report.sort_values('Percentage', ascending=False).head(10))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nNo missing values found.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Data Cleaning Completed.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "afd1f1bd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.3 Feature Engineering\n",
    "We create a new dataframe with additional engineered features. This involves binning continuous variables and creating simplified categories."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "71c7ad88",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Target Variable:** First, we create the target variable `only_medicaid` based on insurance indicators and then drop all original `HINS` columns. We want to predict, whether an individual is insured *only* with Medicaid, and no other insurance type."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 72,
   "id": "4f36dab9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_2_3 = df_2_2.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "insurance = [\"HINS1\",\"HINS2\",\"HINS3\",\"HINS5\",\"HINS6\",\"HINS7\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_2_3[\"only_medicaid\"] = np.where(\n",
    "    (df_2_3[\"HINS4\"] == 1) & df_2_3[insurance].eq(2).all(axis=1),\n",
    "    1,\n",
    "    0\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_2_3 = df_2_3.drop(columns=[c for c in df_2_3.columns if c.startswith(\"HINS\")])\n",
    "\n",
    "target = 'only_medicaid' # save as variable 'target' for function calls later"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "78e24dc3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Group 1 (Income & Affordability):** We introduce the feature `income_group` by binning continuous income, add the boolean variable `has_wage_income`, create `income_source_count` to capture how many income sources an individual has, and add `has_self_employment` to indicate self-employment income."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 73,
   "id": "becb7c5b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# income_group\n",
    "if 'WAGP' in df_2_3.columns:\n",
    "    bins = [-1, 15000, 30000, 50000, 75000, np.inf]\n",
    "    labels = ['Very_Low', 'Low', 'Medium', 'High', 'Very_High']\n",
    "    df_2_3['income_group'] = pd.cut(df_2_3['WAGP'], bins=bins, labels=labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "# has_wage_income\n",
